7	import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException;
8	
9	/**
10	 * Rejects creating an owner that duplicates an existing one, so the create endpoint responds 409
11	 * instead of storing a duplicate. Two rules, both keyed off the deterministic household:
12	 *
13	 * <ul>
14	 *   <li><strong>Exact identity duplicate</strong> — the new owner's whole identity key
15	 *       ({@code normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId}, see
16	 *       {@link OwnerIdentity}) equals an existing owner's. This is genuinely the same person and is
17	 *       always rejected.</li>
18	 *   <li><strong>Household duplicate</strong> — the new owner shares an existing owner's household,
19	 *       i.e. the same {@code householdId} computed from {@code (lastName, postcode)}. Because the
20	 *       household is now keyed on {@code (lastName, postcode)}, a second owner with the same last name
21	 *       and postcode is the same household and is rejected — <em>unless</em> the request opts in with
22	 *       {@code sharesHousehold: true}, which bypasses this block so the owner is created as a declared
23	 *       household member.</li>
